            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0382" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3527/2–1247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-12T17:00:00-04:00">February 12,
                            1947—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>137. Argentine Embassy has submitted for consideration of Bolivian Government
                    proposed Argentine–Bolivian bilateral air transport agreement. Captain Pol,
                    Director Civil Aeronautics Ministry Defense, informed Embassy that text of
                    agreement generally similar to that of proposed US–Bolivia agreement except that
                    there is a provision for control of frequencies. Embassy will attempt to secure
                    copy of agreement’s text from Foreign Office for forwarding to Department.</p>
                <p>Repeated Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
